                <pb facs="0609" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1614: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-27T11:00:00-05:00">April 27, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Department’s No. 94, April 12, 6 p.m. The following telegram has been
                    received from Bogotá:</p>
                <p>(Here quote telegram No. 46, April 21, 5 p.m., from Bogotá.)</p>
                <p>This formula seems to provide an eminently fair and reasonable settlement of the
                    Leticia affair and you may informally so inform Lester.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
